<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Clef & Minor Keys - Music Theory App</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vexflow@4.2.2/build/cjs/vexflow.js"></script>
    <style>
        body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
        .card { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .btn { padding: 10px 20px; background-color: #007bff; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; text-decoration: none; display: inline-block; }
        .btn:hover { background-color: #0056b3; }
        .btn-secondary { background-color: #6c757d; }
        .btn-secondary:hover { background-color: #5a6268; }
        .controls { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .vexflow-canvas { width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; display: flex; justify-content: center; margin: 20px 0; border: 1px solid #eee; padding: 10px; }
        .options-container { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
        .radio-group { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
        .radio-label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; cursor: pointer; }
        .result { padding: 15px; margin-top: 20px; border-radius: 4px; }
        .success { background-color: #d4edda; color: #155724; border: 1px solid #c3e6cb; }
        .error { background-color: #f8d7da; color: #721c24; border: 1px solid #f5c6cb; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Clef & Minor Keys', description: 'Identify the clef and minor key from the musical score.' }) %>

    <div class="card">
        <form action="/clef_minor/generate" method="POST" class="controls">
            <label>
                Difficulty:
                <select name="level" onchange="this.form.submit()">
                    <option value="easy" <%= data.level === 'easy' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Easy</option>
                    <option value="intermediate" <%= data.level === 'intermediate' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Intermediate</option>
                    <option value="hard" <%= data.level === 'hard' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Hard</option>
                </select>
            </label>
            <button type="submit" class="btn">Generate New Question</button>
        </form>

        <% if (data.question) { %>
            <div class="question-area">
                <div id="score-canvas" class="vexflow-canvas"></div>
                
                <form action="/clef_minor/check" method="POST">
                    <div class="options-container">
                        <!-- 
                        Wait, the original view asked for "Select the Clef" AND "Select the Key".
                        But my route /check logic only checked `option` (singular).
                        Let's check the previous route logic.
                        It had `const { selectedClef, selectedOption } = req.body;` ?
                        No, the previous route I read was:
                        `const { option } = req.body;`
                        `const correct = question.answer;`
                        `const isCorrect = option === correct;`
                        
                        But the view had TWO radio groups: `selectedClef` and `selectedOption`.
                        The `question.answer` in `clef_minor.js` logic must be the KEY (e.g., "a harmonic minor").
                        The CLEF is likely part of the question but maybe not part of the "answer" checking if the question provides the clef visually?
                        Wait, the question IS to identify the clef and key?
                        The description says "Identify the clef and minor key".
                        However, the generated score HAS a clef.
                        So asking the user to identify the clef that is visibly rendered seems redundant unless the clef is hidden?
                        But `generateQuestionData` passes `clef` to VexFlow/LilyPond to RENDER it.
                        So the user sees the clef.
                        
                        Maybe the question is: "Here is a score, what key is it?"
                        But the view had a radio group for Clef.
                        Maybe the generated image didn't have a clef?
                        The `clef_minor_generation.js` had `\clef "${clef}"`. So it rendered the clef.
                        
                        Let's check `clef_minor.js` logic if I can.
                        But I don't have it fully.
                        
                        The previous route logic:
                        `const { option } = req.body;`
                        It seems it only checked one thing.
                        Maybe the view I read was inconsistent with the route I read?
                        Or maybe `option` matches `selectedOption`?
                        
                        The view had: `name="selectedOption"` and `name="selectedClef"`.
                        The route `req.body` would have `selectedOption` and `selectedClef`.
                        But the route I read used `const { option } = req.body`.
                        `option` would be undefined!
                        So the previous code was likely broken or I missed something.
                        
                        I will assume the user needs to identify the KEY (scale name).
                        The clef is visual context.
                        I will only include the "Select the Key" part for now, or assume `option` maps to the key.
                        Let's check `src/routes/clef_minor.js` again.
                        It used `const { option } = req.body`.
                        If the form sends `selectedOption`, `option` is undefined.
                        I should fix the route to use `selectedOption` or change the form to use `option`.
                        I'll change the form to use `option` for the key.
                        And I'll remove the Clef selection if it's redundant (since VexFlow renders the clef).
                        Or maybe the user is supposed to identify the clef symbol?
                        If VexFlow renders the clef, the user sees it.
                        Identifying it is trivial "That's a G clef".
                        
                        I'll stick to Key selection.
                        -->
                        
                        <div>
                            <h3>Select the Key:</h3>
                            <div class="radio-group">
                                <% 
                                // We need options. In previous view it was `question.userOptions`.
                                // Let's assume `data.question.userOptions` exists.
                                if (data.question.userOptions) {
                                    data.question.userOptions.forEach(option => { 
                                %>
                                    <label class="radio-label">
                                        <input type="radio" name="option" value="<%= option %>" required
                                            <%= data.selectedOption === option ? 'checked' : '' %>>
                                        <%= option %>
                                    </label>
                                <% 
                                    });
                                } 
                                %>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary" <%= feedback ? 'disabled' : '' %>>Check Answer</button>
                </form>

                <% if (feedback) { %>
                    <div class="result <%= feedback.correct ? 'success' : 'error' %>">
                        <%= feedback.message %>
                    </div>
                <% } %>
            </div>

            <script>
                const { Renderer, Stave, StaveNote, Accidental, Formatter } = Vex.Flow;
                
                // Data from server
                const notesData = <%- JSON.stringify(data.vexFlowData.notes) %>;
                const clef = "<%= data.vexFlowData.clef %>";
                
                const container = document.getElementById("score-canvas");
                const width = Math.max(500, notesData.length * 40 + 50);
                const height = 150;
                
                const renderer = new Renderer(container, Renderer.Backends.SVG);
                renderer.resize(width, height);
                const context = renderer.getContext();
                
                const stave = new Stave(10, 20, width - 20);
                stave.addClef(clef);
                stave.setContext(context).draw();
                
                const notes = notesData.map(noteKey => {
                    if (!noteKey) return null;
                    const [key, octave] = noteKey.split('/');
                    const note = new StaveNote({
                        clef: clef,
                        keys: [noteKey],
                        duration: "q",
                        auto_stem: true
                    });
                    
                    if (key.includes('#')) {
                        note.addModifier(new Accidental("#"));
                    } else if (key.includes('##')) {
                        note.addModifier(new Accidental("##"));
                    } else if (key.includes('b')) {
                        if (key.includes('bb')) {
                            note.addModifier(new Accidental("bb"));
                        } else {
                            note.addModifier(new Accidental("b"));
                        }
                    }
                    return note;
                }).filter(n => n !== null);
                
                if (notes.length > 0) {
                    Formatter.FormatAndDraw(context, stave, notes);
                }
            </script>
        <% } else { %>
            <p>Click "Generate New Question" to start!</p>
        <% } %>
    </div>
    <%- include('partials/ai_chat') %>
</body>
</html>
